30,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, transport costs are huge! We should pick something that doesn't cost a fortune to move or needs its own supports.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"Our staffing is critically low in conservation, and our volunteers are very specialized in local history. We cannot afford a high-maintenance show.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Shion,,The data is clear: visitors want movement and human interaction. Static displays of cased objects are simply not what brings people back.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The suspended bay has strict weight limits, and our evening hires mean we can't have fragile, open installations that can't be secured.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shizue,,I'm afraid we've had too many delays with distant lenders and too many breakdowns with powered displays. We should be cautious.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, if the volunteers love local history, maybe a local theme would work? It might save on those scary transport costs too!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"That is a rational point, Mio. A local focus would align with our current volunteer strengths and reduce the burden on the lab.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Local or not, it must be dynamic. If it's just old pots in boxes, the head counts will drop. We need a ""living"" element.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, ""dynamic"" often means powered displays or heavy rigging. We must remember the weight limits and the risk of damage during evening events.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka is right. The maintenance logs show that powered displays often fail, leaving us to apologize to visitors at the door.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Mio,,Maybe something with people demonstrating things? That's dynamic but doesn't need a motor!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Having people present would satisfy the visitor demand without overloading our depleted technical staff.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shion,,As long as it isn't boring. The comment slips specifically mention wanting to see someone working or talking.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Asuka,,A demonstration-based show would be lighter on the floors and easier to clear for evening hires than a massive installation.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"And if the materials are local, we avoid the nightmare of shipping cut-offs and missing paperwork from overseas.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Mio,,It sounds like we're all leaning toward something local and interactive!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Victoria,,Indeed. It is the only sustainable choice given our current staffing crisis.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Shion,,I will support any candidate that prioritizes engagement over static display.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree, provided the physical requirements are modest.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It seems we have found a peaceful consensus.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
